WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.560
They apply three coats of
oil paint, allowing for

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.750
hours of drying time
between coats.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.690
This is a key step
because aside from

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.270
providing the background
color, the oil paint

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:12.800
waterproofs the paper.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.160
Next, they varnish the
handle to make it

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.570
moisture resistant.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.550
And now for the grand
finale.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.120
An artist paints a
design in vibrant,

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.710
waterproof oils.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.070
The themes are
traditional flowers,

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.900
animals, landscapes,
people.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:40.300
No stencils to trace or
patterns to follow.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.600
The artist works
entirely freehand, the

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.240
result being that no two
umbrellas are ever

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:47.590
exactly alike.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.210
Each oil paper umbrella
is a portable work of

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.920
art. Pretty yet
practical.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.470
Rain or shine.

